{
  "__comment": "Carved wall plaque, PORTRAIT. Built from real depth rather than a picture on a slab: an oak backboard, four forged-iron corner brackets standing proud of it, a raised aged-brass inner frame, the plan sheet sunk behind that frame, and a status lamp in the gap below. PLAQUE-2 step 3 opened the frame out from 5.4x7.4 to 7.4x8.3 so the sheet can carry readable text, moved the brackets clear of the sheet's corners, and lifted the lower rail off the lamp. Modelled facing NORTH; the blockstate rotates it. Depth runs z=16 (against the wall) outward to z=11.6. The sheet face sits at z=12.9 -- the number PlaqueRenderer.SHEET_Z is derived from.",
